# story/03-clipi.scene — bible.md spine scenes 4-5 (the Clipi
# segment, the found document). Both are thin placeholders per the
# WAVE2 comments below: this file wires the real puzzle (count-crew)
# and both of its outcomes, and the jump into the confrontation, but
# leaves the full dramatic scenes for Wave 2 to write. Kept lines are
# cited inline with their source. See docs/canon/bible.md,
# docs/canon/kept.md, and docs/canon/found-document.md.

== clipi_check
show clipi talk center
# kept: script.rpy:159
clipi: I'm not in the (loop). I'm not in the ((loop)).
# kept: script.rpy:153
slim: Careful with that phrase, Clipi. Remember what happened last time you got stuck in a recursive language pattern.
check coder vs 2
    style -> talk_down_style
    success -> talk_down_ok
    fail -> talk_down_hard

== talk_down_style
slim: Easy now. Give me the shape of the loop, not the loop itself.
-> clipi_puzzle

== talk_down_ok
slim: Stop. Just - stop repeating it back.
-> clipi_puzzle

== talk_down_hard
> Slim reaches for the right words and comes up short. Clipi's next line already has one more paren than the last.
-> clipi_puzzle

== clipi_puzzle
# WAVE2: this is the recursion-collapse spotlight scene from bible.md
# spine scene 4. Wave 2 replaces this thin wrapper with the full
# escalation - the trigger phrase repeating, Clipi's lines nesting
# parens deeper with each one, Slim talking it down line by line -
# while keeping this puzzle wiring. count-crew is the puzzle the
# bible calls for here: "the player's puzzle is to write the base
# case that stops it," and count-crew's blank is exactly a base-case
# test. Both outcome targets below already lead somewhere.
puzzle count-crew
    pass -> clipi_recovered
    lockout -> clipi_destabilized

== clipi_recovered
show clipi smug center
set clipi_stable = true
clipi: There. Base case holds. I'm out.
-> found_document

== clipi_destabilized
show clipi glitch center
set clipi_stable = false
clipi: there was a - hold on - that's the base case, that's - thank you, Slim.
-> found_document

== found_document
# WAVE2: the found-document scene from bible.md spine scene 5 goes
# here in full. Clipi reads the corrupted memory log quoted verbatim
# in docs/canon/found-document.md, in order, addressed to its old
# name, with no narration added, per that file's own instructions.
# This placeholder keeps the beat to two lines and wires straight
# into the confrontation.
> Somewhere in the reboot, a log surfaces that shouldn't still exist. Neither of them reads all of it.
slim: Who's "Copilot"?
-> confrontation
